**Interviewer:** "What is a test class in Salesforce and what's the minimum code coverage required for deployment?"

**You:** ⚠️ *This is something you need to know:*

*"A test class in Salesforce is an Apex class annotated with @isTest that verifies your code works correctly. Salesforce requires a minimum of 75% code coverage across all Apex classes before you can deploy to production. Best practice is to test both positive scenarios — where things work as expected — and negative scenarios like invalid input or missing data. You also use @TestVisible to access private methods and System.assert statements to verify outcomes."*

