**Interviewer:** "What is a sandbox and what types are there?"

**You:** ⚠️ *Know this:*

*"A sandbox is a copy of your Salesforce org used for development and testing without affecting production. There are four types: Developer sandbox — smallest, no data copy, good for coding. Developer Pro — slightly larger storage, still no data copy. Partial Copy — copies a sample of production data, good for testing. Full sandbox — exact copy of production including all data, used for final UAT before deployment. At Ridgelinez we worked in sandboxes and deployed to production using change sets."*

